# 🔮 Oracle Vulnerabilities

## Overview

Oracles provide external data (prices, randomness, off-chain events) to smart contracts. Manipulating oracle data is one of the most profitable attack vectors in DeFi.

---

## 1. Spot Price Manipulation

### Using AMM Reserves Directly

```solidity
// VULNERABLE - spot price from Uniswap
contract VulnerableLending {
    IUniswapV2Pair public pair;
    
    function getCollateralValue(uint256 amount) public view returns (uint256) {
        (uint112 reserve0, uint112 reserve1,) = pair.getReserves();
        uint256 price = (reserve0 * 1e18) / reserve1;  // MANIPULABLE!
        return amount * price / 1e18;
    }
}

// ATTACK:
// 1. Flash loan massive amount of token0
// 2. Swap to manipulate reserves → price spikes
// 3. Borrow against inflated collateral
// 4. Repay flash loan with borrowed funds
// 5. Profit when price returns to normal

// SECURE - use Chainlink or TWAP
import "@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/interfaces/AggregatorV3Interface.sol";

contract SecureLending {
    AggregatorV3Interface public priceFeed;
    
    function getCollateralValue(uint256 amount) public view returns (uint256) {
        (, int256 price,,,) = priceFeed.latestRoundData();
        require(price > 0, "Invalid price");
        return amount * uint256(price) / 1e8;
    }
}
```

